<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Weil der Stadt</h1><p class="st-meta">1275 CE – 1802 CE (approx.) · capital Weil der Stadt</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small Catholic imperial city surrounded by Protestant Württemberg, best known as the birthplace of the astronomer Johannes Kepler.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weil-der-stadt">Weil</a> grew on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurm-nagold">Würm</a> west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a> and belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a>, whose estates in the area passed to the Empire on their fall. It was then treated as an imperial city, confirmed in the 1270s, around 1275, its name, Weil the City, distinguishing it from nearby villages.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> ruled this small town with its handful of villages. It lived from farming, crafts and markets. Surrounded entirely by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-wurttemberg">Duchy of Württemberg</a>, it often quarrelled with its powerful neighbour and remained Catholic when Württemberg turned Protestant. The astronomer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-kepler">Johannes Kepler</a> was born there in 1571. Much of the town was burned in 1648 near the end of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years War.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Württemberg finally annexed the town in 1802, ending its long resistance to its neighbour. It is now a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-kepler">Kepler</a> museum in the house where the astronomer was born.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/free-imperial-city-of-weil-der-stadt.jpg" alt="Free Imperial City of Weil der Stadt" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. MarkusHagenlocher assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WdSt-PeterundPaul.jpg" target="